# Clearing a verification-debt row by RUNNING the native gate the row names.
#
# The fixture drives the REAL `le commit debt-clear` against a scratch checkout
# and judges the LEDGER it leaves behind. The row it holds is one no gate can
# re-run, so nothing is run for it and it must stay open: a row is cleared by a
# gate that passed, never by asking. It also drives the cut grammar,
# `debt-clear part <n> of <m>`, in the one form that answers without running a
# gate: `part` with no `of` names no piece count, so it is refused.
#
# Both halves of the gate-exit decision, green and red, are proved by
# TestDebtClearingHonorsTheGateExit (internal/le/commit/commit_test.go), which
# names its own action dispatcher. Through the real dispatcher each of them is a
# native verification run, which claims this machine's job slots, so no
# functional scenario may start one.

option=timeout:value=60s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture runner/verify-scope-debt-clear
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=debt-fixtures-ready
expect=stdout:contains=native-debt-clear-runs-registered-gates
expect=stdout:contains=unrunnable-row-named-and-left-open
expect=stdout:contains=half-named-cut-refused
expect=stdout:contains=debt-clear-started-no-gate
